{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots show the 3D scene rendered cleanly in Chrome with no blank screen or errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 show orbiting and zooming via OrbitControls, and the code restricts `maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465` and `maxDistance = 15.5`, preventing the camera from going below the cloth (`y = 0`) or outside the 34x34 cloth.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "Scene geometry is modest (~80k triangles total across toast, fruit, plate, cloth, and instanced sugar), with two shadow maps (2048 and 1024) and lightweight post-processing (BokehPass and UnrealBloomPass), which will run at 30+ fps on a typical laptop.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All five screenshots display a bottom UI pill (`#ui`) containing text ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom') and interactive buttons ('Macro DoF: ON' and 'Hero Angle'), plus a loading text overlay in the HTML.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "In the `animate()` loop in the source code, only `controls.update()`, camera reset lerping, and DoF focus distance updates occur; there is no environmental motion at all.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows a close-up camera view from slightly above with the stack of French toast centered on the plate, matching the reference photo's framing and angle.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 5 clearly show three slices of French toast stacked on top of one another and slightly rotated/offset, matching the photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show banana slices tucked between the toast layers, on top, and resting on the plate around the base of the stack.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show a cluster of blueberries on top of the stack as well as blueberries scattered around the base on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack resting on a dark round plate set atop a grey-brown linen cloth, though a black void is visible above the cloth horizon.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show white specks scattered across the plate and sparse specks on top of the toast representing powdered sugar.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the toast slices have uniform, exaggerated wavy/scalloped edges all the way around like giant biscuits or crackers rather than thick cut slices of bread with a natural rounded crust and cut edges.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show round banana discs with a faint, darker 3-part seeded pattern in the center, though several slices have severe dark circular rendering artifacts around their rims.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 3, and 4 show plump, slightly varied round blueberries with distinct 5-pointed indented calyx crowns.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 2, a blueberry on the middle-right edge and banana slices visibly intersect/clip rather than resting naturally, and in screenshot 1 the middle and top toast slices hover/cantilever stiffly with gaps.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2, 3, 4, and 5 show complete, closed meshes for the back/sides of the stack, plate, and cloth with no missing faces, though zoomed out (screenshot 5) shows the cloth edge against a black background.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the code (`keyLight.position.set(-5.2, 8.4, 5.4)`) and screenshot 1, the main key light comes from the front-left rather than behind-left, and the syrup lacks bright warm specular highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1, despite `BokehPass` being enabled (`maxblur: 0.0065`), the back rim of the plate and the tablecloth behind it remain nearly sharp rather than softly blurred as in the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1 and 4, several blueberries on top and in the foreground lack soft contact shadows where they meet the toast and plate, appearing pasted onto the surfaces.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1 (and 2, 3, 5), the top strip above the tablecloth horizon is completely black (`#000000` / `#161412` void).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1, 3, and 5, the syrup rivulets on the toast sides and puddles on the plate look like opaque, dull brown paint or plastic tubes rather than glossy, translucent amber liquid with bright specular highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast has smooth, plastic-like vertex-colored orange-brown gradients and vertical fluted ridges with no porous bread crumb texture.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the blueberries have harsh, high-contrast blotchy white/grey noise textures that look marbled rather than a subtle, dusty matte wax bloom with soft highlights.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the banana slices look flat and chalky/opaque, with dark grey metallic-looking ring artifacts around their outer bevels (caused by environment reflection/normal issues on the bevels) rather than moist, slightly translucent fruit.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the plate shows a dark ceramic sheen (though with a sharp circular ring artifact on its floor), while the cloth behind it looks like blurry low-frequency grey-beige stucco/clouds rather than a crisp woven linen fabric.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the plate and tablecloth resting level on the horizontal plane with no unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "Inspecting `addCrustSyrupRivulets` and `animate()` in the code shows the syrup tubes are completely static meshes with no dripping or running animation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "There is no steam or warm haze particle system or shader anywhere in the HTML source or visible in the screenshots.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no environmental motion implemented in `animate()` at all, so no motion runs or loops.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "Although `createBlueberry` varies vertex displacement slightly, all blueberries share the exact same `berryTex` UV texture map (`createBlueberryTextures`), making identical blotch patterns visible on adjacent berries in screenshots 1 and 4.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1, 2, and 3 clearly show banana slices and blueberries intersecting and clipping directly into the toast meshes and into each other (e.g., top banana slice buried halfway into the top toast slice in screenshot 2 and 3, middle berry clipping into toast in screenshot 2).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the sugar on the plate consists of large, uniform, stark-white polka-dot blobs/pebbles (`IcosahedronGeometry(0.015)`) rather than fine powdered sugar.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks unmistakably like stylized/plastic 3D CGI—with cracker-shaped toast, blotchy berries, dark-rimmed clipping bananas, opaque brown syrup tubes, coarse white dots, and a UI bar—and could not pass for the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
